‘Do you call that a shirt?’ I said to my brother.
‘You needn’t be so critical,’ my brother answered as he looked at himself in the mirror.
I sat down on one of those modern sofas and waited.
We had been in the clothing store for half an hour and my brother was still in front of the mirror.
‘We shouldn’t buy things we don’t need,’ I remarked suddenly.
I regretted saying it almost at once. ‘You needn’t have said that,’ my brother answered.
‘I need not remind you of those shoes you bought last week.’
‘I find them comfortable,’ I said.
‘A man can never have too many shoes.’
‘And a woman can’t have too many dresses,’ he answered.
Ten minutes later we walked out of the store together.
My brother was wearing a shirt that looked like a circus tent!